Origin statement
-----------------
Software English is a controlled natural language for software and
systems engineering prose. Its design is informed by publicly known
structural mechanisms of controlled-language systems in general (a
restricted vocabulary, one sense per word, simple grammar, short
sentences) as described in public secondary sources about the field of
controlled natural languages.

Software English does not copy, reproduce, adapt, or derive from the
text, word lists, writing rules, or any other copyrighted material of
ASD-STE100 (Simplified Technical English), which is the property of ASD
(AeroSpace and Defence Industries Association of Europe). No ASD-STE100
text, dictionary, or rule document was consulted or used in building
Software English's vocabulary or rule catalogue. General, publicly
available secondary descriptions of the structural shape of controlled
natural languages as a field — for example an encyclopaedia entry noting
that Simplified Technical English pairs a grammar-rule component with a
separate closed dictionary component — were read to understand the
genre, not to source Software English's content. The name "Simplified
Technical English" and its abbreviation are not used to describe
Software English, and Software English claims no relationship to the
ASD-STE100 specification.

Software English's vocabulary and rule set are built from scratch for
software and systems engineering prose, and are independently licensed
as stated in LICENSE.
